1. The grid is divided into 3×3 blocks separated by rows/columns of 5s.
2. Exactly one block contains no 8 — this is the "template" block.
3. Each output block (i,j) is filled entirely with the value found at relative position (i,j) within the template block.

Verified across all examples — the block without 8 acts as a map determining what value fills each block in the output.

